-- THE COST OF QUALIFYING, ASSERTED.  Two aliases, each naming its own module's
-- `Node`, so the two use sites are spelled apart and resolve sees no collision
-- among its import-local names.  The collision is downstream: the alias prefix
-- is stripped before typecheck, whose constructor table is keyed by the bare
-- name and would keep whichever import folded last.  Both spellings are rows,
-- because nothing in the program says which of the two the author meant to win.
import ca as A
import cb as B

x : A.TA
x = A.Node 1

y : B.TB
y = B.Node 2
